==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|cu|ru}} {{term|людиє|sc=Cyrs|lang=cu}}, from {{etyl|sla-pro|ru}} {{term/t|sla-pro|*ljudъ}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ru}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*h₁lewdʰ-o-||men, people}}. Compare English ''[[lede#Etymology 2|lede]]'', Old Norse {{term|lýðr|lýðir|people|lang=non}} (Icelandic {{term|lýður|lang=is}}), Gothic {{term|𐌻𐌹𐌿𐌸𐍃|tr=liuþs|lang=got}}, German {{term|Leute|lang=de}}, Ancient Greek {{term|ἐλεύθερος|lang=grc|tr=eleutheros}}, Latin {{term|līber|lang=la}}, {{term|līberī|lang=la}}.

